---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Mechveck"
	description="Research-driven guides to AI tools and productivity software"
	pubDate={new Date('January 11 2026')}
>
	<p>
		<strong>Mechveck</strong> publishes research-driven comparisons of AI tools and
		productivity software. We dig through reviews, documentation, and user discussions
		so you don't have to.
	</p>

	<h2>Our Approach</h2>
	<p>
		We believe in transparency. Our comparisons are based on:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Verified user reviews</strong> - G2, Capterra, TrustRadius, and Reddit discussions</li>
		<li><strong>Official documentation</strong> - Pricing pages, feature lists, and changelogs</li>
		<li><strong>Real user feedback</strong> - Forums, communities, and published case studies</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Every claim is backed by sources you can verify yourself. We'll tell you where
		the information came from, not just what we concluded.
	</p>

	<h2>What We Cover</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>AI Writing Tools</strong> - Content generation, email automation, copywriting</li>
		<li><strong>Productivity Software</strong> - Project management, note-taking, collaboration</li>
		<li><strong>Tool Comparisons</strong> - Side-by-side analysis with cited sources</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Why This Matters</h2>
	<p>
		Too many "review" sites claim to test products they've never used. We take a
		different approach: thorough research with honest attribution. You'll know
		exactly where our information comes from.
	</p>

	<h2>Stay Updated</h2>
	<p>
		Check back for new research reports and comparisons.
		Find us on <a href="https://github.com/mechveck">GitHub</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
